    // Day-scale calibration (2026-07-18): 0.08/inference gave a companion 6-8
    // conversational exchanges from a full tank — she tired fastest exactly when
    // most engaged. 0.004 prices a heavy day (~60 solo identity inferences plus
    // tool steps at half rate) at about half the post-sleep budget; the passive
    // drain (VitalityState.TICK_ENERGY_RATE) covers the other half. All hardcoded
    // act costs below were rescaled 1/20 with it so proportions held.
    private static final double ENERGY_DRAIN_PER_INFERENCE = Double.parseDouble(
        System.getenv().getOrDefault("WYRDSEKAI_ENERGY_DRAIN", "0.004"));
    // Bonded recovery (2026-07-18, the "a bit better than human" half of the
    // calibration): an exchange TRIGGERED BY A HUMAN partially pays for itself,
    // scaled by live rapport — warm company is restorative, an eroded bond isn't.
    // At rapport 0.75 a typical exchange (reply + a tool step or two) nets to a
    // slight drain, so an evening of good conversation is sustainable while solo
    // grinding still tires. Gated on the trigger being a human (not self, not an
    // agent peer, not a cross-zone agent tell), so it cannot be farmed
